\title{delphyr: Reproducible Round-Based Delphi Studies}
\description{
Validated study protocols, deterministic consensus classification and
longitudinal analysis of round-based Delphi studies, with transactional
study services backed by 'PostgreSQL'.
}
\section{Offline analysis}{

Needs neither a database nor the application. \code{\link[=new_protocol]{new_protocol()}} and
\code{\link[=new_scale]{new_scale()}} validate the declarative study configuration,
\code{\link[=new_snapshot]{new_snapshot()}} freezes the submitted answers of a round under a content
hash, \code{\link[=analyse_round]{analyse_round()}} classifies consensus with explicit denominators
and missingness, \code{\link[=compare_rounds]{compare_rounds()}} describes paired change between
comparable rounds and \code{\link[=prepare_feedback]{prepare_feedback()}} applies small-cell suppression.
\code{\link[=reproduce_export]{reproduce_export()}} and \code{\link[=reproduce_study_export]{reproduce_study_export()}} verify a research
export and recompute its analysis. \code{vignette("offline", package = "delphyr")} is the worked example.
}

\section{Study services}{

The services work on a 'PostgreSQL' database reached through
\code{\link[=connect_repository]{connect_repository()}} and prepared with \code{\link[=migrate_repository]{migrate_repository()}}. Each
service checks identity, study membership, capability and state again and
signals a structured condition, see \code{\link[=del_abort]{del_abort()}}. \code{\link[=demo_study]{demo_study()}} creates
a synthetic study for development and tests.
}

\section{Scope}{

The bundled examples use synthetic data only. Consensus thresholds in
\code{\link[=demo_protocol]{demo_protocol()}} are examples, not recommendations. Production use
requires the documented security and operational acceptance gates.
}

